backward_ros: declare _Unwind_Backtrace() on QNX

backward.hpp walks the stack with _Unwind_Backtrace() from <unwind.h>.
QNX's <unwind.h> declares it (and _Unwind_Trace_Fn) only under _GNU_SOURCE,
which ROS builds do not define: "'_Unwind_Backtrace' was not declared in
this scope". Declare the two for QNX; libgcc_s has the function.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/include/backward_ros/backward.hpp b/include/backward_ros/backward.hpp
index 93037d5..86426ed 100644
--- a/include/backward_ros/backward.hpp
+++ b/include/backward_ros/backward.hpp
@@ -375,6 +375,13 @@ typedef SSIZE_T ssize_t;
 #if BACKWARD_HAS_UNWIND == 1
 
 #include <unwind.h>
+#if defined(__QNX__) && !defined(_GNU_SOURCE)
+// QNX's <unwind.h> declares _Unwind_Backtrace() only for _GNU_SOURCE.
+extern "C" {
+typedef _Unwind_Reason_Code (*_Unwind_Trace_Fn)(struct _Unwind_Context *, void *);
+extern _Unwind_Reason_Code _Unwind_Backtrace(_Unwind_Trace_Fn, void *);
+}
+#endif
 // while gcc's unwind.h defines something like that:
 //  extern _Unwind_Ptr _Unwind_GetIP (struct _Unwind_Context *);
 //  extern _Unwind_Ptr _Unwind_GetIPInfo (struct _Unwind_Context *, int *);
